IMPORT prelude

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore) -- digging near telecommunication cables (Part 5, ss 33 to 36) and the offences of
-- Part 6 that reach ordinary people and contractors: unlicensed systems and radio equipment (ss 53 to 55), seizure and
-- forfeiture (s 57), using an unlawful service (s 59), interference with messages (ss 61, 62), fraudulent use (ss 63, 64),
-- damage to plant and compensation (ss 66, 68, 69).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TA1999.txt (amendments to
-- Act 25 of 2021).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 23 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to offences and duties that bind
-- people other than licensees. Not encoded: the exclusive privilege and licensing (Part 2), entry on land (Part 3), codes
-- and directions (Part 4), control of designated licensees (Part 5A), special administration (Part 5B), dispute resolution
-- (Part 5C), and the general penalty section (so penalties are given only where the offence section states its own).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Telecommunications Act 1999 -- offences`

§§ `33 to 36 -- digging near cables`

-- s 33(1): no earthworks "within the vicinity of any telecommunication cable" unless (a) at least 7 days' written notice to the
-- licensee, (b) cable location information obtained and the licensee consulted, and (c) "telecommunication cable detection
-- work" done by a LICENSED cable detection worker. (2): except where reasonably believed necessary for public or private
-- safety -- then written notice within 7 days AFTER. (6): $100,000 or 3 years. (7): defence of all reasonable steps or due
-- diligence.
-- s 35(2): an unlicensed detection worker "is not entitled to recover in any court any charge, fee or remuneration".
-- s 36: digging "with any mechanical equipment or explosive" without first ascertaining cable locations -- $100,000 or 3
-- years. Hand digging is outside s 36 (but not outside s 33).
DECLARE Earthworks HAS
    `near a telecommunication cable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave 7 days written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained cable information and consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used a licensed cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believed urgent for safety` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave notice within 7 days after starting` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the works` IS AN Earthworks
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the earthworks comply with section 33` IF
    IF NOT `the works`'s `near a telecommunication cable` THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the works`'s `reasonably believed urgent for safety`
         THEN `the works`'s `gave notice within 7 days after starting`
         ELSE     `the works`'s `gave 7 days written notice`
              AND `the works`'s `obtained cable information and consulted`
              AND `the works`'s `used a licensed cable detection worker`

GIVEN `used machinery or explosives` IS A BOOLEAN, `ascertained the cable locations first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the digging is a section 36 offence` IF
    `used machinery or explosives` AND (NOT `ascertained the cable locations first`)

GIVEN `is a licensed cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee recoverable for detection work` MEANS
    IF `is a licensed cable detection worker` THEN `the fee` ELSE 0

§§ `68, 69 -- damaging plant`

-- s 68(1): "wilfully" removing, destroying or damaging telecommunication plant -- a fine up to $50,000 or 3 years.
-- (2): "Despite subsection (1)", anyone who "in the course of carrying out any earthworks, DAMAGES OR SUFFERS TO BE DAMAGED any
-- cable" -- a fine up to $1 MILLION or 5 years. No mental element; (4) defence of all reasonable precautions and due
-- diligence. (3): the employer or principal is liable too, unless it proves no consent or connivance and no neglect.
-- s 69(1): whoever damages plant "whether wilfully, negligently, accidentally or otherwise" pays compensation as well.
--
-- Cutting a cable by accident while digging carries twenty times the maximum fine of cutting it on purpose with a pair of
-- pliers.
DECLARE Damage IS ONE OF
    `wilful damage outside earthworks`
    `damage to a cable during earthworks`
    `accidental damage outside earthworks`

GIVEN `the damage` IS A Damage, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the damage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the damage`
    WHEN `wilful damage outside earthworks` THEN 50000
    WHEN `damage to a cable during earthworks` THEN (IF `proved due diligence` THEN 0 ELSE 1000000)
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the damage` IS A Damage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is payable for the damage` IF TRUE

GIVEN `the employer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the damage was attributable to the employer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable for the employee's cable damage` IF
    `the employer consented or connived` OR `the damage was attributable to the employer's neglect`

§§ `53 to 57 -- unlicensed systems and radio equipment`

-- s 54(1): no one may sell telecommunication equipment, or POSSESS radio-communication equipment, except under a licence or
-- the regulations.
-- s 55(2): a person in possession of radio-communication equipment "is deemed, until the contrary is proved, to have operated
-- the same". (3): the OCCUPIER of premises where unlicensed radio equipment is installed commits an offence; (4) unless they
-- were not aware and could not with reasonable diligence have become aware.
-- s 57(3): seized equipment not prosecuted is forfeited "unless a claim is made within 2 months after the date of seizure".
GIVEN `possesses the radio equipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved it was not operated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possessor is taken to have operated it` IF
    `possesses the radio equipment` AND (NOT `proved it was not operated`)

GIVEN `unlicensed radio equipment installed on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not with reasonable diligence have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier commits an offence` IF
    `unlicensed radio equipment installed on the premises` AND (NOT `could not with reasonable diligence have known`)

GIVEN `prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `claim made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized equipment is forfeited` IF
    (NOT `prosecuted`) AND (NOT `claim made`) AND `months since seizure` GREATER THAN 2

§§ `59 to 64 -- using services and messages`

-- s 59: using a system "knowing or having reason to believe" it was set up in contravention of the Act.
-- s 62(1)(b): a licensee's employee who intercepts, detains or disconnects a message commits an offence, except on a Minister's
-- order or court direction, and (2) except for installation and maintenance work or "the tracing of the origin of any
-- telephone call at the request of the subscriber".
-- s 64: possessing or supplying any thing for the dishonest obtaining of a service -- up to $100,000 or 10 YEARS.
GIVEN `knew or had reason to believe it was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the unlawful service is an offence` IF
    `knew or had reason to believe it was unlawful`

DECLARE Interception IS ONE OF
    `reading a customer's messages out of curiosity`
    `acting on a Minister's order`
    `acting on a court direction`
    `routine maintenance`
    `tracing a call at the subscriber's request`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Interception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee commits a section 62 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `reading a customer's messages out of curiosity` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `intends dishonest use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for possessing a fraud device` MEANS
    IF `intends dishonest use` THEN 10 ELSE 0
